window.THERAPIES={Abdominal:"Abdominal Therapy",Acupressure:"Acupressure",Ashiatsu:"Ashiatsu",Buccal:"Buccal Therapy",Craniosacral:"Craniosacral Therapy",Cupping:"Cupping Therapy",Deep:"Deep Tissue",Energetic:"Energetic Healing",Graston:"Graston Technique",KT:"KT Tape",Lymphatic:"Lymphatic Drainage",Myofascial:"Myofascial Release",Neuromuscular:"Neuromuscular",Prenatal:"Prenatal Massage",Reiki:"Reiki",Reflexology:"Reflexology",Scar:"Scar Recovery",Scrape:"Scrape & Tape",Sports:"Sports",Stretching:"Stretching",Swedish:"Swedish",TMJ:"TMJ"};window.therapists=[{name:"Robin Barbee",bio:["Director and Owner of Franklin Massage Center, Robin brings 25 years of experience in advanced therapeutic massage and sports recovery. She is committed to providing highly specialized care for athletes and active individuals across Franklin, Brentwood, and Nashville.","A 2000 graduate of the Tennessee School of Massage Therapy in Memphis, Robin has developed a unique, clinically focused approach that integrates Deep Tissue Massage, Cupping Therapy, Graston Technique, and targeted mobility work to enhance athletic performance, speed recovery, and prevent injury.",'Robin has worked with professional athletes from the NFL, NBA, NHL, and MLB, as well as Ironman competitors, marathoners, endurance runners, and collegiate athletes, including the Lipscomb University softball team. Her reputation for precision bodywork and deep understanding of athletic biomechanics has earned her the trust of many in the sports community. In 2017, she was voted Best Massage Therapist by "Nashville Fit Magazine".',"Robin works closely with Berry Hill Chiropractic and Wellness and Nashville Physical Therapy to ensure a comprehensive and collaborative approach to athletic care and rehabilitation."],therapies:[THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Cupping,THERAPIES.Graston,THERAPIES.Sports,THERAPIES.Swedish,THERAPIES.TMJ]},{name:"Mallory Barbee",bio:["Mallory graduated from the Nashville School of Massage in 2017. As a life-long athlete, she recognized that pursuing a career in massage therapy would allow her to help clients achieve their fitness goals while minimizing the risk of injury. Over the past eight years, Mallory has worked with a diverse clientele, including professional athletes from the NFL, NHL, and MLB, as well as stylists, surgeons, teachers, and individuals seeking relaxation.","Mallory has developed a deep passion for cupping therapy and its healing benefits on the body. While cupping is one of her preferred modalities, she also specializes in deep tissue, Swedish, sports massage, and relaxation techniques. Each session is tailored to meet the specific needs of her clients, often incorporating a combination of different modalities.","Known for her attentive nature, Mallory actively listens to her clients and assesses their unique needs. She customizes each session based on their condition that day, focusing on pain management and overall well-being. ","Beyond her professional pursuits, Mallory enjoys spending quality time with her wife, son, and their three dogs. She is also an avid fan of MMA, and when she is not engaged in woodworking or home improvement projects, she can often be found watching MMA events. Mallory looks forward to meeting new clients and building lasting relationships with them!"],therapies:[THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Swedish,THERAPIES.Sports,THERAPIES.Cupping]},{name:"Kate Wicks",bio:["I'm a graduate of the Nashville School of Massage Therapy and have had the privilege of working with athletes at all levels—from high school to professional—supporting them in injury prevention, recovery, and overall pain management. My practice is centered around helping each individual enhance their athletic performance and build long-term resilience through improved flexibility, range of motion, and movement tailored to their specific sport. I draw from a variety of techniques, including neuromuscular therapy, cupping, and fascial stretching, to create a personalized approach that meets each client's specific goals."],therapies:[THERAPIES.Cupping,THERAPIES.Graston,THERAPIES.Lymphatic,THERAPIES.Myofascial,THERAPIES.Neuromuscular,THERAPIES.Prenatal,THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Swedish,THERAPIES.Sports,THERAPIES.TMJ]},{name:"Victoria Wares",bio:["I offer an elevated approach to bodywork that feels as good for your nervous system as it does for your muscles. My sessions blend artistry and advanced technique to create true depth through awareness, not force. Every touch is intentional, and every movement is designed to bring your body into harmony.","My work focuses on smart, effective depth — the kind that melts tension and encourages lasting release without strain or pain. Using Ashiatsu, cupping, and warm stone therapy, I reach deep layers safely and intuitively, allowing your body to unwind at its own pace.","I'm also a certified Manual Lymphatic Drainage therapist, offering gentle, rhythmic treatments that support post-surgical recovery, detoxification, and overall balance. These sessions help restore the body's natural flow, leaving you lighter, clearer, and deeply relaxed.","Clients describe my touch as fluid, intuitive, and transformative — a blend of skill and sensitivity that invites deep calm and renewal."],therapies:[THERAPIES.Ashiatsu,THERAPIES.Graston,THERAPIES.Cupping,THERAPIES.Acupressure,THERAPIES.Lymphatic,THERAPIES.Swedish,THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Sports]},{name:"Jessica Sowards",bio:["Based in Nashville, I offer integrative bodywork designed to deliver effective, results-driven care tailored to each client. With training from Cumberland Holistic Therapies, I incorporate techniques such as deep tissue work, facial therapy, and therapeutic scraping to support muscular release, improved function, and overall well-being.","Each session is thoughtfully customized, addressing both the structural and energetic aspects of the body. My approach is attentive, intuitive, and focused on helping clients move better, feel better, and maintain long-term wellness.","I am currently expanding my practice through the study of Healing Touch energy work to further support balance, relaxation, and the body's natural healing process."],therapies:[THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Swedish,THERAPIES.Graston,THERAPIES.Craniosacral,THERAPIES.Acupressure]},{name:"Tripp Vaughn",bio:["Hello, I'm Tripp! I graduated from Bluewater Institute for Massage Therapy in Killen, Alabama, in early 2024. With 15 years of experience as a cheerleading coach, I bring an understanding of movement, muscular demands, and the importance of recovery to my massage practice.","I specialize in therapeutic, deep tissue, and sports massage, incorporating cupping and Graston instrument-assisted soft tissue techniques to address muscular tension, soft tissue restrictions, and mobility concerns. I tailor each session to your needs, whether you're managing ongoing discomfort, recovering from training, or seeking relaxation.","My approach combines targeted bodywork with a comfortable, welcoming experience to help you move more freely, recover, and feel your best."],therapies:[THERAPIES.Cupping,THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Graston,THERAPIES.Prenatal,THERAPIES.Sports,THERAPIES.Swedish]},{name:"Craig Elliott",bio:["Hello, I'm Craig! As a veteran and former athlete, I understand the demands that training, work, and everyday life place on the body. With five years of experience serving clients across the Nashville area, I specialize in therapeutic massage focused on relieving chronic muscular tension, improving mobility, and supporting recovery.","My approach combines targeted soft tissue work with an understanding of how muscle tension and movement patterns can contribute to discomfort. I work with you to identify areas of concern and tailor each session to your needs, comfort level, and physical goals.","Whether you're managing ongoing tension, recovering from physical activity, or seeking greater ease of movement, my goal is to help you move more comfortably and feel your best."],therapies:[THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Myofascial,THERAPIES.Prenatal,THERAPIES.Sports,THERAPIES.Swedish]},{name:"Tiffany Gerald",bio:["Hi, I'm Tiffany! I graduated from the Nashville School of Massage Therapy in 2025 and am passionate about helping clients feel their best through personalized massage care. I offer deep tissue, sports, prenatal, and relaxation massage, tailoring each session to your needs and comfort level.","With nine years of experience teaching Barre fitness, I bring a strong appreciation for movement, strength, and the mind-body connection to my practice. My approach focuses on easing muscle tension, supporting recovery, and encouraging overall wellness.","My goal is to create a welcoming environment where you feel comfortable and cared for. Whether you're maintaining an active lifestyle, navigating pregnancy, or simply making time for yourself, I'm here to help you feel refreshed and renewed."],therapies:[THERAPIES.Prenatal,THERAPIES.Lymphatic,THERAPIES.Cupping,THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Sports]},{name:"Hanna Fleming",bio:["Hi, I'm Hanna! I graduated from the Nashville School of Massage in March 2026, where I trained in therapeutic massage and bodywork. I earned my certification in equine massage therapy in 2021, and my hands-on experience working with horses deepened my understanding of anatomy, muscle function, and mobility.","I tailor each massage to your goals and comfort level. Whether you're looking to ease muscle tension, move more comfortably, or take time to unwind, we'll talk about what you'd like to focus on and adjust the session based on how you feel.","My goal is to provide a welcoming environment where you feel comfortable asking questions, sharing feedback, and taking time to care for yourself."],therapies:[THERAPIES.Lymphatic,THERAPIES.Cupping,THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Sports]},{name:"Jazmine Smith",bio:["Hi, I'm Jazmine! I graduated from Mind Body Institute in 2024 and specialize in deep tissue massage, prenatal massage, and cupping therapy. My approach focuses on your individual needs, comfort, and wellness goals, with each session tailored to help relieve muscle tension, encourage relaxation, and support overall well-being.","I strive to create a warm, welcoming environment where you feel comfortable and cared for. Whether you're seeking targeted tension relief, support during pregnancy, or time to recharge, my goal is to help you leave feeling renewed."],therapies:[THERAPIES.Prenatal,THERAPIES.Cupping,THERAPIES.Deep,THERAPIES.Sports]}];